{
  "id": "the-missing-route",
  "name": "The Missing Route",
  "category": "routing",
  "difficulty": 4,
  "xp": 350,
  "level": 5,
  "description": "Two routers, one link, and neither knows about the other side.",
  "brief": "The branch office and head office are joined by a point-to-point link on 10.0.0.0/30. Both routers are cabled and both have addresses.\n\nA router only ever knows the networks it is directly attached to. Router-01 has never heard of 192.168.20.0/24, and Router-02 has never heard of 192.168.10.0/24.\n\nAdd a static route on each router so packets can find their way there and back.",
  "hints": [
    "Run 'show ip route' on both routers and compare what is missing.",
    "On Router-01 add: 192.168.20.0 / 255.255.255.0 via 10.0.0.2",
    "On Router-02 add: 192.168.10.0 / 255.255.255.0 via 10.0.0.1",
    "One route alone is not enough — the reply needs a way home too."
  ],
